# Frontier drought flag

**Status: ON**

This is the standing switch. Behaviour lives in `model-routing.mdc`. Do not probe
frontier models to “check” whether this is still true.

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **ON** | Cursor Other Models is empty, or Matthew declared drought. Never spawn Sol, Opus, Sonnet, or Kimi. |
| **OFF** | Frontier pool has credit. Use the canonical pins in `model-routing.mdc`. |

## How Matthew sets it

Say one of these; a write-capable agent flips **Status** on this page.

- **ON:** “Drought is ON” · “frontier is dry” · “out of Other Models” · “stop using Sol/Opus”
- **OFF:** “Drought is OFF” · “credits are back” · “frontier is back”

## How agents set it

- Write-capable agents **must** flip this to **ON** when Matthew uses an ON phrase, or when a Task / `@` spawn fails with `Other Models usage limit reached`.
- Write-capable agents flip this to **OFF** only when Matthew uses an OFF phrase (or he explicitly tells them to). A lucky frontier spawn is **not** a refill.
- Readonly heads (Clive, Pam, and other read-only lanes) treat the current **Status** as binding and do not edit this file.

Once **ON** in a conversation, it stays ON for that conversation even if someone forgot to save the file. Do not retry spent models.
